# L §5.18: "diff(e) in S against B: e evaluated in world S and in world B"; L §6.1 the reality is all its files; L §6.4
# reads of scenario items are allowed in diff. s1 and s2 are each over hh (two stacks): salary at law 2027-06-30 is
# 6 000.00 in s1 and 4 000.00 in s2 (each replaces the base's row on its span, L §4.6 step 2). (Was
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §6.4, writer 5's T-96, stated.) The layout is this interpreter's (diff, as for d2).
=== hh.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-11-15
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input salary: money PLN

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  salary = 5 000.00 PLN "umowa"

ask d: diff(salary) in s1 against s2 law 2027-06-30
ask d2: diff(salary) in s1 against hh law 2027-06-30
=== s1.tally
scenario s1 over hh
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version a
  cite s
  governs 2027-01-01..
  known 2026-10-20
  replace salary = 6 000.00 PLN "s1"
=== s2.tally
scenario s2 over hh
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version b
  cite s
  governs 2027-01-01..
  known 2026-10-20
  replace salary = 4 000.00 PLN "s2"
=== expect
d: diff in s1 against s2: 1 changed, 0 added, 0 removed, 0 unchanged
  changed salary: 6 000.00 PLN against 4 000.00 PLN
...
d2: diff in s1 against hh: 1 changed, 0 added, 0 removed, 0 unchanged
  changed salary: 6 000.00 PLN against 5 000.00 PLN
...
